    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="0764" n="652" xml:id="pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-14T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 14,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:32
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2793. Following from [Cole at] Archangel.</p>
                <p>“1379, August 13, 8 p.m. I have received official notification of the changes in
                    the Government reported in my 1375, August 12, 7 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >6</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d732-f1"/> and am replying that I feel
                    assured that the Government of the United States will be favorably impressed by
                    the participation in the Government accorded to representatives from elective
                    bodies such as the Provincial Zemstvos and the Archangel Municipality as well as
                    by the institution of a labor inspector to facilitate peaceful solution of
                    industrial advantages [<hi rendition="#italic">problems?</hi>]. Cole.[”]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d732-f1" n="56" xml:id="d732-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted in telegram from the Ambassador in Great Britain, no. 2791, Aug. 14,
                    6 p.m., <ref target="#pg650">p. 650</ref>.</p>
            </note>
